From 8bd9619f7aee4a0a9e67db5b339241f327727bca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: beardedeagle <randy@heroictek.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:02:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(filters): don't print a TOML filter's on_empty message
 when the command failed

A TOML filter captures stdout only unless it sets filter_stderr, and stage 8
printed on_empty whenever that stdout filtered away. A failed command's stdout
is often empty for exactly that reason: its errors go to stderr. So
`rtk mix compile` on a broken project printed the compiler error on stderr and
then `mix compile: ok` on stdout, while exiting 1.

on_empty now fires only when the command exited zero. A failed run whose
stdout filters away prints what is left (nothing, or the raw stdout when the
recovery hint would cost more), and stderr and the exit code are unchanged.
`rtk verify` and inline [[tests.*]] still exercise the success path.
